// Approver Who is ASKED FIRST when something must be signed off for you — an agent asking permission, a
// task nobody touched in time, a spend over your limit. Anyone whose role allows approving may
// also sign, and an Owner always can (decision 0558), so nothing waits on this one person. It is
// the approver in the environment this credential acts in; in a personal environment it is you,
// or a guest you nominate (`setMyApprover`).
// **Never empty**, because "waiting for approval" with nobody named is how work dies quietly.
type Approver struct {
	Name string `json:"name"`

	// PersonId A UUID version 7 (RFC 9562) — sortable by creation, and never a counter.
	//
	// Examples: 019250e1-8f3c-7c21-9a4d-3a2f7b6c1d90
	PersonId Id `json:"person_id"`

	// Username Your ONE identifier: you sign in with it and other people find you by it. LOWERCASE ONLY
	// (decision 0561): lowercase letters, digits, dot, underscore and hyphen. A capital is refused,
	// never lowered on a caller's behalf — the capitals a person wants shown belong in `name`.
	//
	// Examples: jonas.vh
	Username Username `json:"username"`
}

// Audience WHO CAN SEE ONE THING ON YOUR PROFILE CARD. **Public** — anyone, signed in or not. **Team** —
// the people you share a company with. **Guests** — the outside people working with you, who
// are neither your team nor the public. **Private** — nobody but you.
//
// `team` IS REFUSED IN A PERSONAL ENVIRONMENT (422 naming the field): such an environment has
// guests and has no teams, and nobody meets a word for a thing they do not have (Jonas,
// 2026-09-25). The default is `team` in a company and `private` in a personal environment —
// the second ruled by Jonas on 2026-10-04 ("nobody but you", decision 0680), after the Profile
// Visibility page had carried it as asked and not picked.
//
// HIDDEN MEANS REFUSED, THE LINK INCLUDED. This is a FLOOR under the access system, not a
// hint to a client: a detail hidden from someone is not reachable by opening its address
// either, so the server leaves it out of every answer to them rather than trusting a caller
// to honour the value it reads here. Roles and shares still decide what may be reached inside
// an app; they cannot lift this floor.
//
// Four values, settled 2026-09-25, after the screen and the configuration line had each named
// a different three for months. The word AUDIENCE is this and only this — choosing which
// customers get a capability first is a release decision and borrows no vocabulary from here.
type Audience string

// BaselineAudience One of the four `Audience` words, or `default`: the page's default, the whole company (`team`).
// `default` is stored as nothing, so a member left on it follows the page's default if that ever
// changes. For a team, `default` is no say at all: the team's members follow their other teams.
type BaselineAudience string

