// €19.99 to a person, a customer's program and an agent alike, with no rule to know first. The
// amount is a decimal written as a STRING, never a JSON number, so it is exact and is never
// rounded on its way through a parser. It carries exactly the currency's own decimals — two for
// EUR, none for JPY — and is never negative: a refund or a credit says its direction in the
// field's name. Until 2026-10-07 this was a whole number of cents, exact but unreadable without
// the rule (ONPLO-1737).
