	// CastCompanyFeatureVote Cast the company's vote for a future feature
	//
	// The company's one vote on a feature an app has decided to build later, cast in its business
	// environment, beside each person's own (decision 1034). Whoever holds the permission casts it:
	// the built-in Administrator, or a role the company gives it. Two people casting it are the
	// company's one vote. An agent may draft the company's vote for a person to cast, and never
	// casts it itself.
	//
	// VOTING AGAIN IS THE SAME VOTE. A second vote on the same feature, by anybody in the company,
	// changes nothing and answers the vote as it was first cast. There is no second vote to refuse,
	// and so no 409.
	//
	// EVERY VOTE IS PRIVATE. The answer is this company's own vote and nothing else: never another
	// company's, never who in the company cast it, and never how many members it has. A parent's
	// Administrator who came into a daughter through its family link is refused 403
	// `through_family_link`, because a parent never learns whether its daughter voted.
	//
	// A PERSON CASTS IT. The vote is speech in the company's name, so a machine's or an agent's
	// credential is answered 404 `subject_not_person`, as a person's own vote is.
	//
