	// with an end. You link their identity and store no contact. The role is one that app may
	// grant on an object, Viewer by default, and on its own it grants only Free features. Normally
	// done from the object's own Share panel, which calls this.
	//
	// THE SHARE IS A GRANT IDENTITY KEEPS (decision 0861): any Onplo person may be given one, and
	// being a guest is nothing but holding one here. Identity also asks whether you may share that
	// object at all, by the object's own app, so this act needs that and `guest-grant.create` both
	// (decision 0658).
	//
	// SHARING AGAIN CHANGES THE SHARE THAT IS THERE. A person holds one grant per object (decision
	// 0650), so a person shared with again takes the new role and the new end and keeps the id.
	// `created` says which it was, and the status is `200` either way.
	//
	// `access_until` IS THE MOMENT THE SHARE ENDS, and the time zone it was chosen in (decision
	// 0650). A share with a guest always ends: the guest defaults set how long a screen offers
	// first. A moment that has already passed is refused (422 naming `access_until`).
	//
	// Takes any type of body and a specified content type.
	//
	// Corresponds with POST /guest-grants (the `ShareWithGuest` operationId).
