	// AskAccountDeletionWithBody Delete your account, after a wait you choose
	//
	// Asked from your personal environment, after "Are you sure?" names the day. The wait is
	// yours to choose, from none to 30 days, and you can cancel during it. The day itself is when
	// the account is deleted; everything erasable is then erased within 30 days.
	//
	// **A FRESH PASSKEY SIGN-IN CONFIRMS IT.** A sign-in from earlier in the day is not enough:
	// without a recent proof the answer is `passkey_proof_required`, and proving again clears it.
	//
	// WHEN IT IS ASKED, you are signed out on every device, this one included, and one mail goes to
	// the address Onplo writes to, naming the day and saying that signing in cancels nothing by
	// itself: signing in during the wait asks whether to keep deleting or cancel. The mail carries
	// no link that cancels.
	//
	// Your work in a company stays the company's. The last Owner of a company is refused
	// (`last_owner`) until they make someone else one.
