	//
	// EXACTLY ONE ADDRESS IS THE ONE ONPLO WRITES TO, and marking another unmarks it — the server's
	// job, never the caller's, as `updateSignInMethod` does for the Primary sign-in method. Only a
	// VERIFIED address can be marked, because Onplo never writes to one that is not.
