// SetCompanyUsernameWithBody Change the company username
//
// Its own operation for the reason a person's username has one: the rules travel with it. A
// company username is unique across the whole platform, usernames included (one @ name space,
// decision 0793), changeable at most once every 30 days, and the old one stays out of anyone's
// reach for 90 days. Nothing breaks when it changes: every agent and machine keeps its id, and
// only the username it is shown by follows. Asking for the company username the company already
// holds changes nothing and answers 200, so a retry whose answer was lost is not refused as too
// recent.
//
// A company made before company usernames existed sets its first one here (ONPLO-3449); that
// first one starts no 30 days. Answered in a Business Environment only; a personal environment
// has no company, and answers 404.
//
// "COMPANY USERNAME" is the word a person reads for a company's @ name (decision 0974).
//
