// UpdateFamilyLinkWithBody Set the link's takeover switches
//
// Pays the bills (with the daughter's monthly ceiling and approval threshold), pushes policies,
// sees usage and compliance, and admin access. Every switch is off until set, visible on both
// sides, revocable and logged. ONLY THE PARENT TURNS ONE ON, AND EITHER SIDE TURNS ONE OFF: a
// takeover is the parent's to ask for, and "revocable" means the daughter can always take it back.
// Derived admin access can never create or change role assignments for itself, and changes
// nothing of the daughter's side of the link (decision 0830). What a parent's Administrator does
// inside the daughter is logged there like everyone's, and no separate message is sent.
//
// AN AMOUNT IS SET OR TURNED OFF: a ceiling or a threshold set to an amount it did not hold is
// turning it on, and `null` turns it off. An amount with more decimals than its currency has is
// a 422 naming the field. Naming a switch at the value it already holds changes nothing and is
// never refused.
//
// WHAT A SWITCH DOES ARRIVES LATER. Today a switch is held, shown on both sides and logged, and
// it changes nothing else yet: the parent gains no access, pushes no policy and sees no usage in
// the daughter, and no bill is paid from the parent's method.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type.
//
// Corresponds with PATCH /family-links/{family_link_id} (the `UpdateFamilyLink` operationId).
