	// CompleteProfilePhotoUploadWithResponse Make the bytes you sent your profile picture
	//
	// THE PICTURE IS YOURS FROM THIS MOMENT, and not before. The store reads what arrived at the
	// address, and only then is it kept: your profile answers the new picture, the previous one
	// becomes a previous version, and the bytes count toward your quota.
	//
	// WHAT ARRIVED IS JUDGED, NEVER WHAT WAS CLAIMED. Nothing at the address yet is
	// `upload_incomplete`, and the upload stays open to be sent. Bytes that come to another size
	// than the start declared are `size_differs`: the cap and the space were judged on that size,
	// so a picture of another size is one nobody agreed to. Bytes that are not one of
	// `allowed_media_types` are `media_type_not_allowed`, whatever the upload said they were.
	//
	// A REFUSED COMPLETION LEAVES YOUR PICTURE EXACTLY AS IT WAS. Nothing is half-kept.
	//
	// ASKING TWICE IS SAFE. Completing an upload that is already complete answers the same
	// picture and changes nothing, so a completion whose answer was lost is simply sent again.
	//
	// AN UPLOAD THAT IS NOT YOURS, WAS NEVER STARTED, OR WAS SWEPT answers `not_found`, the same
	// for all three: which of them it was is not something a caller is told.
	//
	// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
	//
	// Corresponds with POST /me/photo/{upload_id}/completion (the `CompleteProfilePhotoUpload` operationId).
