	//
	// Identity-first lookup across every environment (`onplo.account.control-center.users`): "find
	// a person by username, or by an email that may match several, and see their environments, sign-in
	// methods, devices and sessions — never a credential and never their content", as the catalogue
	// says it. Exactly one of `username` and `email` is sent; both or neither is a 422.
	//
	// A USERNAME FINDS AT MOST ONE PERSON, because signing in is username-only and the username is
	// the one identifier. AN EMAIL MAY FIND SEVERAL: an address is a contact detail, never an
	// identity, and the same one can sit on a personal and a business account, so the answer is a
	// list and the operator picks. An email matches only a confirmed address. Nobody found is an
	// empty list, never a 404.
	//
	// Each row's environments are Account's own facts: which environment, and the person's
	// membership state there. Never their roles, never anything inside.
	//
	// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
