	//
	// "End every session a person has, in every environment, at once" — the catalogue's sentence,
	// from `onplo.account.control-center.users`. The person signs in again on their next request;
	// nothing they made is touched.
	//
	// THE SESSIONS ARE THE IDENTITY SERVICE'S, and it ends them (`RevokeAllSessions` in
	// `api-contracts/identity/proto/credentials.proto`); no session of the caller's survives on the
	// person's behalf, because the caller holds none of theirs.
	//
	// THE REASON IS ASKED because every act the Onplo team takes ON an environment writes an entry in
	// that environment's own activity naming the action and the reason, and notifies its owner
	// (`onplo.account.control-center.audit-logs`). It travels in the body, never the address, so it
	// stays out of every log that records a request's address. Each request ends every session there
	// is at that moment, so it is safe to send twice.
	//
	// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
	//
	// Corresponds with POST /platform/people/{person_id}/session-revocations (the `RevokePlatformPersonSessions` operationId).
