// SendInvitationsWithBodyWithResponse Invite one person or many
//
// One address or many (decision 0459): every row becomes an invitation. Teams and direct roles
// are chosen once for the batch, and a row may carry its own in their place, so one person can
// be made an Administrator in the same batch. With no teams chosen anywhere, they join Everyone. Each invited address is mailed a link that lives 14 days;
// the mail opens Onplo and signs nobody in (decision 0198).
//
// THE BATCH IS ANSWERED ROW BY ROW, in the order sent. A row for somebody already a member here,
// or already invited, is not sent and says so; every other row is. `checkInvitations` asks the
// same question without sending anything, for the dialog that shows the list before it is sent.
//
// WHAT IS NOT HERE YET: Premium seats chosen before sending — the seats' operations are
// ONPLO-1649's. Accepting is the invited person's, from their own side: `acceptInvitation`.
