// ListInvoicesWithResponse Every invoice this environment has been charged
//
// Newest first, each carrying its own state. An invoice is a record, so it is never removed:
// paid, failed and settled rows all stay, and the state is written on the row rather than
// deciding whether the row exists. A failed one says why, and when the next try is. In a company
// whose parent pays its bills, an invoice stays this company's own and shows who settled it: a
// payer is not an owner.
//
// AN INVOICE'S PDF is `POST /invoices/{invoice_id}/download-address`, and the fix a failed
// one asks for is `POST /payment-method/replacements`. Charging a failed one again now is
// `POST /invoices/{invoice_id}/retries`.
