// StartProfilePhotoUploadWithBodyWithResponse Ask for somewhere to put your profile picture
//
// THE BYTES NEVER COME THROUGH THIS API. A picture is a file at System / Account / Profile in
// your own storage (decision 0396), in the zone only the owning app may write. So Account asks
// Storage to make a place for it and hands you back the one address that may write there:
// single use, short-lived, and refusing anything larger or of another type.
//
// SAY HOW LARGE IT IS AND WHAT IT IS BEFORE A BYTE MOVES. The size is held against the largest
// a picture may be and against the space you have left, here, at the door: a picture over the
// cap is refused with `file_too_large` and one that does not fit with `quota_full`, never
// discovered when the last byte arrives.
//
// SEND THE BYTES TO THAT ADDRESS, THEN COMPLETE THE UPLOAD. Until
// `POST /me/photo/{upload_id}/completion` answers, your picture is the one it was: the store
// keeps nothing until it has read what really arrived, and the completion is where you are
// told. This paragraph said "then you are done; nothing has to be confirmed afterwards" until
// 2026-10-02. A picture that was refused then had nobody to tell: the bytes were sent, the
// sender was told nothing, and the picture never appeared (ONPLO-1029). An upload you never
// complete costs nothing — the file answers as absent and the quota it used is zero.
//
// IT IS NOT A FIELD ON `PATCH /me/profile`, and not a body on this operation either. Account
// is a record service: ten megabytes of your face passing through it on the way to the store
// is work nothing in this path should do, and the read already proved the primitive — one
// short-lived scoped address, two directions.
//
// REPLACING KILLS THE OLD ONE AT ONCE, the moment the completion answers. The previous picture
// becomes a previous version under the ordinary versioning rules, and any address already
// issued for it stops resolving — so a face taken down cannot be fetched a minute later by a
// page that still holds its address.
//
// IT COSTS YOUR QUOTA, current version and history alike. There is no free-history loophole
// for a profile picture.
//
// WHO SEES IT IS NOT A CHOICE HERE (Jonas, 2026-09-27). A picture is as visible as your name:
// whoever can already see your profile card sees it, which is why the photo does not join
// `ProfileVisibility` beside `email` and `phone`. A hidden face would make every screen that
// shows people fall back to initials for one person, and that has to look deliberate rather
// than broken.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /me/photo (the `StartProfilePhotoUpload` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) StartProfilePhotoUploadWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*StartProfilePhotoUploadResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.StartProfilePhotoUploadWithBody(ctx, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseStartProfilePhotoUploadResponse(rsp)
}

